# =========================================================================
# manager.bcyr — what a hierarchical crew's manager costs (ADR 035).
#
# No oracle: the Rust line ran a hierarchical crew sequentially. A file of its own, as the roadmap's
# 2.7.1 asks of crew rows, so what ran before a row does not move it. The crew is `orch.bcyr`'s
# `_b_o_spec` with four tasks, run sequentially and then managed by `a1`, so the two crew rows
# differ by the manager alone: three workers instead of three agents, a copy of each within its
# manager's tools, and one more call, the manager's answer, handed every worker's.
#
# Stdlib is auto-prepended from cyrius.cyml — do NOT include stdlib modules.
# =========================================================================

